In article <20587.26ebf78d@psuecl.bitnet> jrb@psuecl.bitnet writes:
>Second, I just started playing around with the Samurai class a bit, and
>one of my characters started with a weapon called a "wakizashi."  Does
>anyone out there know what the heck a "wakizashi" is?

A "wakizashi" is a Japanese short sword, traditionally used by the Samurai
as a secondary weapon and for ceremonial purposes.  It has an extremely
sharp blade (Japanese swords are among the finest in the world) of about
seventeen inches.  The blade curves slightly upward, and the blade comes
to a sharp point suitable for thrusting.

One of the uses of the wakizashi (if I have all my facts straight) was for
committing hari-kiri, or ceremonial suicide.  The point would be inserted
into the stomach, and then the blade would be brought upward toward the
rib cage.  Preferably, an honorable companion would then use his katana, 
or long sword, to behead the person committing suicide.  (It would be a
pretty slow any painful death, otherwise.)

